# MaCSad read-only development gateway

The gateway serves the generated administrative bundle and one safe health read.
There are deliberately no mutation routes. The first typed command endpoint must
wait for authorization, idempotency, optimistic concurrency, PostgreSQL, events,
and outbox writes to exist as one tested transaction boundary.

## To isHealthRoute (method: Text, path: Text) -> Bool:
    If method is equal to "GET":
        Return path is equal to "/api/v1/health".
    Return false.

## To mutationRouteAvailable (routeKnown: Bool) -> Bool:
    Return false.

## To handle (request: Request) -> Response:
    If request's method is equal to "GET":
        If request's path is equal to "/api/v1/health":
            Return plain("MaCSad gateway ready | persistence: not connected | mutations: disabled").
    Return notFound().

## Test: Health route is classified
    Let safeRoute be isHealthRoute("GET", "/api/v1/health").
    Let unsafeRoute be isHealthRoute("POST", "/api/v1/health").
    Expect that safeRoute is equal to true.
    Expect that unsafeRoute is equal to false.

## Test: Mutation routes are unavailable
    For all booleans routeKnown:
        Let available be mutationRouteAvailable(routeKnown).
        Expect that available is equal to false.

## Main
Serve on port 18081 with handle.
